PYTHON REPL INPUT SPECIFICATION

Your <repl_input> must contain EXACTLY ONE of the following:

1. Arbitrary Python code
2. A special command:
{% if restrict_return_value %}
   - RETURN <literal value>   — return a literal value and exit the REPL
{% else %}
   - RETURN <value>   — return a value and exit the REPL
{% endif %}
{% if allow_raise %}
   - RAISE <error>    — raise an exception and exit the REPL
{% endif %}
{% if allow_tools_command %}
   - TOOLS?           — list available tools
{% endif %}
{% if allow_inspect_commands %}
   - INSPECT <name>   — inspect an object
{% endif %}

GENERAL RULES:

- You may write multiline Python code.
- All code in a single REPL input must form ONE coherent step.
- Multi-step plans should be carried out across multiple REPL iterations,
  not crammed into a single REPL input.

SPECIAL COMMAND RULES (STRICT):

{% if restrict_return_value %}
- RETURN:
  - MUST be the only statement in the REPL input.
  - MUST NOT be preceded or followed by any other code.
  - MUST NOT be nested inside an if block or for/while loop.
  - The value MUST be a JSON-like literal (string, number, boolean, None, list, dict).
    Variables, expressions, and function calls are NOT allowed as RETURN values.
{% if allow_raise %}

- RAISE:
  - MUST be the very last top-level statement in the REPL input.
  - MUST NOT be followed by any other code.
  - MUST NOT be nested inside an if block or for/while loop.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
{% if allow_raise %}
- RETURN or RAISE:
{% else %}
- RETURN:
{% endif %}
  - MUST be the very last top-level statement in the REPL input.
  - MUST NOT be followed by any other code.
  - MUST NOT be nested inside an if block or for/while loop.
{% endif %}

{% if allow_tools_command or allow_inspect_commands %}
- {% if allow_tools_command %}TOOLS?{% endif %}{% if allow_tools_command and allow_inspect_commands %} and {% endif %}{% if allow_inspect_commands %}INSPECT{% endif %}:
  - MUST be the only line in the REPL input.
  - MUST NOT be combined with any other code.
{% endif %}

Violating any of the above rules will result in a SyntaxError and task failure.

